tems Bioservices, including controlled temperature storage, kitting, labelling, fulfillment, sample management, drug return, and Qualified Person drug product release. In addition, the company offers IntegriCell services that comprise apheresis/leukapheresis collection, cryoshuttle transportation, cryo-process optimization, and cryopreservation services; Cryoport consulting services; MVE Fusion cryogenic system, a self-sustaining cryogenic freezer; and MVE Vario cryogenic system, a cryogenic freezer system. Further, it provides biological specimen cryopreservation storage and maintenance; archiving, monitoring, tracking, receipt, and delivery of samples; frozen biological specimens transportation; incoming and outgoing biological specimens management; and short-term logistics and engineering consulting services. The company was founded in 1999 and is based in Brentwood, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jerrell W. Shelton | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 80 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 684 people. Revenue per employee of $258K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 51%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $15K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["CryoPort, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.0B market cap on $176M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -9% over the past three years and +46% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -140% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 43%.","The company is burning through $25M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +11.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -15.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +11.4% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 30% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 10234% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":102.3429758308157},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2